# Workspace state — tracks, journals, scratch. Never committed.
.worksite/

# The journal mirror. Normally committed so a track can be resumed on another machine; not here.
# The entry header now carries a derived device ALIAS rather than the device name (p8.31), so the
# mirror is no longer the leak it was under p8.8 — but a journal still records what was done on
# which machine and when, and this repo is public, so the journal stays local for this project.
# scripts/check.sh section 5 asserts the .worksite/ rule above; this line has no such check,
# because an untracked mirror is indistinguishable from one that was never created.
docs/agent/journal/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
